claim.claim-text:
(i) protein Rv0601c, derived from a Mycobacterium species or related organism and comprising at least one T-cell epitope;
(ii) an homolog of the protein Rv0601c having an amino acid sequence with at least 80% similarity to the protein Rv0601c after optimal alignment; and
(iii) a peptide fragment of the protein as defined in (i) or (ii), the peptide fragment comprising or consisting of an amino acid sequence selected from ADLVRELVTILPIVLVIAAVAAYLLSR (SEQ ID NO:6), AAYLLSRAALRPVDRIRAAA (SEQ ID NO:7), TTLNTMLTRLQRALAHEQQF (SEQ ID NO:8), DLFVSIDPDHLRRILTAVLDN (SEQ ID NO:9), and SGLGLAIVAALTTTHGG (SEQ ID NO:10);
for a time and under conditions sufficient to stimulate the lymphocytes to produce an effector molecule, wherein the presence or level of the effector molecule is indicative of the lymphocytes derived from a subject infected with or prior exposed to the Mycobacterium species.

(i) protein Rv0601c, derived from a Mycobacterium species or related organism and comprising at least one T-cell epitope;
(ii) an homolog of the protein Rv0601c having an amino acid sequence with at least 80% similarity to the protein Rv0601c after optimal alignment; and
(iii) a peptide fragment of the protein as defined in (i) or (ii), the peptide fragment comprising or consisting of an amino acid sequence selected from ADLVRELVTILPIVLVIAAVAAYLLSR (SEQ ID NO:6), AAYLLSRAALRPVDRIRAAA (SEQ ID NO:7), TTLNTMLTRLQRALAHEQQF (SEQ ID NO:8), DLFVSIDPDHLRRILTAVLDN (SEQ ID NO:9), and SGLGLAIVAALTTTHGG (SEQ ID NO:10);
for a time and under conditions sufficient to stimulate the lymphocytes to produce an effector molecule, wherein the presence or level of the effector molecule is indicative of the subject's capacity to mount a cell-mediated immune response.

(a) the subject is a human or a non-human animal;
(b) the incubation between blood and biomarker occurs in a test-tube;
(c) the incubation occurs further in the presence of heparin;
(d) the incubation occurs further in the presence of an added carbohydrate;
(e) the incubation occurs further in the presence of a Mycobacterium protein or peptide fragment thereof or chemical analog thereof derived therefrom selected from ESAT6, CFP10, TB7.7 and PPD or mixture thereof; and/or
(f) the effector molecule is selected from interferon-γ, a cytokine, an interleukin and TNF-α.

(i) protein Rv0601c, derived from a Mycobacterium species or related organism and comprising at least one T-cell epitope;
(ii) an homolog of the protein Rv0601c having an amino acid sequence with at least 80% similarity to the protein Rv0601c after optimal alignment; and
(iii) a peptide fragment of the protein as defined in (i) or (ii), the peptide fragment comprising or consisting of an amino acid sequence selected from ADLVRELVTILPIVLVIAAVAAYLLSR (SEQ ID NO:6), AAYLLSRAALRPVDRIRAAA (SEQ ID NO:7), TTLNTMLTRLQRALAHEQQF (SEQ ID NO:8), DLFVSIDPDHLRRILTAVLDN (SEQ ID NO:9), and SGLGLAIVAALTTTHGG (SEQ ID NO:10);
and one or more pharmaceutically acceptable adjuvants, carriers, excipients and/or diluents.

(i) protein Rv0601c, derived from a Mycobacterium species or related organism and comprising at least one T-cell epitope;
(ii) an homolog of the protein Rv0601c having an amino acid sequence with at least 80% similarity to the protein Rv0601c after optimal alignment; and
(iii) a peptide fragment of the protein as defined in (i) or (ii), the peptide fragment comprising or consisting of an amino acid sequence selected from ADLVRELVTILPIVLVIAAVAAYLLSR (SEQ ID NO:6), AAYLLSRAALRPVDRIRAAA (SEQ ID NO:7), TTLNTMLTRLQRALAHEQQF (SEQ ID NO:8), DLFVSIDPDHLRRILTAVLDN (SEQ ID NO:9), and SGLGLAIVAALTTTHGG (SEQ ID NO:10);
for use in the treatment or prevention of infection by Mycobacterium species.
